---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Popple — Privacy Policy">
  <section class="container-app py-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy — Popple</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">
      Last updated: <span class="notranslate">October 14, 2026</span>
    </p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert space-y-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Popple (formerly Bubble Match) is a single-player chain-reaction
          puzzle game developed by Jacob. It has no accounts, no sign-in and no
          servers of its own. This policy explains what data the app handles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">2. Data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Locally on your device:</strong> your game progress (daily puzzle
          results, streak, Adventure levels passed, practice position and jokers) and
          your settings (sound, vibration, daily reminder). We, the developer, never
          receive this data.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Android backup:</strong> if backup is turned on in your phone's
          settings, Android may include this game progress in your device backup,
          so it can be restored on a new phone. That backup is stored and managed
          by Google under your Google account; we have no access to it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Through third-party advertising (Google AdMob):</strong> when an
          ad is loaded or shown, Google may collect a device advertising identifier,
          coarse (IP-based) location, device information, and ad interaction data.
          See section 4 below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">3. Permissions</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">INTERNET</code> — required to fetch ads.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code> — used by the
            ad SDK to detect connectivity.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">VIBRATE</code> — used for haptic feedback on
            big chain reactions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">POST_NOTIFICATIONS</code> — optional, for the
            daily reminder (see section 6). You can refuse it or turn the reminder off
            in the game settings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">AD_ID</code> — lets the ad SDK read the
            device advertising identifier.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">4. Third-party services: Google AdMob</h2>
        <p>
          Popple shows <strong>rewarded ads</strong> provided by
          <strong>Google AdMob</strong>, and only when you choose to watch one (for
          example, to get an extra tap in Adventure). AdMob is operated by Google
          LLC and is subject to Google's own privacy practices. The app asks Google
          for ads suitable for a general audience.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Consent:</strong> in the European Economic Area, the UK and
          Switzerland, the app shows Google's consent form before any ad is
          requested, and ads are only personalised if you agree. You can change your
          choice at any time from the game's Settings &rarr; Privacy options.
        </p>
        <p>When an ad is loaded or shown, Google may automatically receive:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>Your device's advertising identifier (Ad ID).</li>
          <li>Coarse location derived from your IP address.</li>
          <li>Device and app information (model, OS version, app version).</li>
          <li>Ad interaction data (impressions, clicks, video views).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">For full details, read:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400"
              href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400"
              href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or
              apps that use our services</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400"
              href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Manage your ad personalization in Google
              Ads Settings</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can reset or delete your device's advertising ID at any time from
          Android Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">5. Sharing your results</h2>
        <p>
          When you tap "Share" after solving the daily puzzle, the app builds a
          short text (puzzle number, taps, a grid of emojis and a link to the game)
          and hands it to the app you pick, such as a messaging app. Nothing is sent
          unless you choose to share, and we never see what you share.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">6. Daily reminder</h2>
        <p>
          If you allow notifications, the app shows one notification in the evening
          when today's puzzle is still unsolved. It is scheduled and decided on your
          device; nothing is sent to a server. Turn it off in the game's Settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">7. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Popple is intended for players aged 13 and over and is not directed at
          children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can erase all local data at any time by clearing the app's storage
          in Android Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; Popple &rarr; Storage &rarr;
          Clear data, or by uninstalling the app. Device backups are managed in
          your Android and Google account settings. For data Google has collected
          through ads, use Google's Ads Settings and Privacy controls linked above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          Any updates to this policy will be reflected on this page with a revised
          "Last updated" date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions? Email
          <a
            class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 notranslate"
            href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
